===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|feed|back<id:rear>|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfiːdˌbæk/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-feedback.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# Critical [[assessment]] of a [[process]] or [[activity]] or of their results.
#: {{syn|en|estimation|assessment|critique|evaluation}}
#: {{ux|en|After you hand in your essays, I will give both grades and '''feedback'''.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Marina Carver|title=Study finds Boston police target African-Americans disproportionately|url=https://www.cnn.com/2014/10/09/us/boston-police-stop-frisk/index.html|date=2014-10-09|passage=“Over the past month, the Department has held three separate meetings with the ACLU to receive '''feedback''' and engage the organization in the solutions,” the department said in a statement. “As a result of the meetings, the Department agrees that publishing FIO statistics going forward is necessary, and the Department is working toward personalizing interactions between officers and citizens.”|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231001233131/https://www.cnn.com/2014/10/09/us/boston-police-stop-frisk/index.html|archivedate=1 October 2023}}
# {{lb|en|electronics|cybernetics|control theory|}} The part of an output [[signal]] that is looped back into the input to control or modify a system.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=w:Oliver Sacks|title=Musicophilia: Tales of Music and the Brain
|passage=The fact that similar cortical abnormalities can be experimentally induced in monkeys has allowed Michael Merzenich and his colleagues in San Francisco to explore an animal model of focal dystonia, and to demonstrate the abnormal '''feedback''' in the sensory loop and the motor misfirings that, once started, grow relentlessly worse.}}
# {{lb|en|amplification}} The high-pitched [[howling]] noise heard when there is a [[loop]] between a [[microphone]] and a [[speaker]].
#: {{syn|en|audio feedback|Larsen effect|howlback|howlround}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=John Griesemer|title=No One Thinks of Greenland|publisher=Picador|isbn=9781466803244
|passage=A loud '''feedback''' screech blasted from a speaker on the wall. It was a hailing signal of some kind.}}

